# Dependencies (this package ships zero runtime dependencies; node_modules only
# ever appears for local tooling and must never be committed).
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
package-lock.json.bak

# Secrets — never commit a gateway key, a DSH profile .env or local settings.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Local DSH state, when someone runs a throwaway profile inside the repo.
# NOTE: the pattern is .dsh/* rather than .dsh/ so that ONE thing inside can be
# un-ignored below. Excluding the directory itself would stop git from descending
# into it, and no negation would ever apply.
.dsh/*
# The project skill is a DELIVERABLE, not local state: it is the carryable part of
# this project's method, and it belongs in the repository so a clone carries it.
# Kept at .dsh/skills/ specifically because that is the path DSH scans for project
# skills — so a plain git clone of this repository puts a working skill in place,
# with no copy step and therefore no second copy to drift.
!.dsh/skills/
profiles/

# Logs and diagnostics.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
logs/

# Test / coverage output.
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# Packed artifacts (npm pack / pnpm pack).
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Build scratch space.
.tmp/
tmp/

# Working notes. `_lead/` is where the investigation behind a release is
# written down: probe scripts, raw responses, reachability measurements,
# design documents. It is a workbench, not a deliverable, and this package is
# published — `git add -A` in the release ceremony would otherwise sweep it
# into the repository silently, which is precisely the failure mode rule 1
# exists to prevent.
#
# The canonical location is the *workspace* `_lead/` (the parent of this
# repository), not a copy inside it. This rule is the backstop for when a
# session writes to the wrong one anyway, which has already happened once.
#
# NOTE: `_lead/flake-probe.mjs` is tracked on purpose (rule 8 cites it as the
# diagnostics for the unresolved intermittent test failure) and is unaffected
# by this rule — gitignore never untracks a file that is already in the index.
_lead/
